  <h2 class="section-title">1 Gallon Flash Boiler + Electronic Water Injection → 440 L/min Steam 90 PSI</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Phase 20 replaces the 15 gallon slow boiler with a 1 gallon flash boiler — only enough water is ever heated to what's immediately needed.
    Electronic Water Injection (EWI) feeds precise micro-doses of water from the 20 gallon external tank into the flash chamber.
    Result: always at pressure, minimal maintenance wattage (~1,000W vs 2,000W+), cold start in ~74 seconds tested.
    Condenser returns exhaust steam back to liquid water, feeding the external tank — approaching closed loop operation.
