  <div class="new-box">
    <h4>▶ PHASE 20 RANGE IMPROVEMENTS</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Condenser loop recovers 70%+ of exhaust steam — water consumption near-zero at steady cruise</li>
      <li>20 gallon tank replaces the 15 gallon boiler as water reserve — 33% more water capacity while saving ~36 kg</li>
      <li>EWI prevents pressure overshoot — no steam wasted through PRV under normal operation</li>
      <li>Flash boiler means no dead water volume sitting at temperature doing nothing — 100% of heated water is in active use</li>
      <li>Theoretical range: unlimited with condenser running. Practical: carry extra for cold climate or hard acceleration runs</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Road Test Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Top speed limited by 200 RPM engine ceiling — 4th gear ~32 MPH. Phase 21 could address with overdrive ratio</li>
      <li>Locked differentials improve traction but increase turning effort — acceptable for low-speed, high-torque application</li>
      <li>250mm stroke pistons deliver significantly more torque per cycle than Phase 19's 120mm stroke — expect ~2× torque improvement</li>
      <li>EWI needs calibration at each operating RPM band — PID tuning is a bench test task before road use</li>
      <li>Condenser efficiency drops in hot ambient conditions — monitor water tank level on summer days</li>
    </ul>
