    <ul>
      <li>Flash boiler runs hotter per unit volume than drum boiler — ceramic blanket insulation mandatory on outer shell</li>
      <li>Condenser outlet water can reach 70°C if overloaded — use SS tank, not HDPE, if condenser return feeds warm water in</li>
      <li>20 gallon water tank positioning: keep away from steam pipe tunnel heat. Under-trunk preferred over tunnel-adjacent</li>
      <li>Static oil bath: no active pump means no oil circulation cooling — external cooler strongly recommended at sustained full load</li>
