  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 20 Stress Notes — 250mm Stroke Is a Big Jump</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>250mm stroke piston rods are significantly longer than Phase 19's 120mm — buckling analysis required on the piston rod under compression at 90 PSI</li>
      <li>250mm ∅ locomotive wheels are large — check that rail engagement doesn't create excessive side load on shaft bearings at 200 RPM</li>
      <li>EWI pressure spikes: if EWI over-injects during cold start, brief pressure surges above 90 PSI are possible — PRV must be tested and confirmed</li>
      <li>Condenser back-pressure: if condenser is undersized, exhaust restriction could increase effective back-pressure on pistons — model exhaust side too</li>
      <li>Static oil bath: without circulation, hot spots near worm-gear mesh could exceed PAO thermal limit locally — thermocouple on each mesh point recommended</li>
    </ul>
