  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 20 Cost Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Flash boiler saves ~$1,700 vs 15 gal drum boiler — major reduction in most expensive single steam component</li>
      <li>Dual alternators add ~$1,600 but replace the single 48V generator + chain multiplier combo — roughly cost-neutral</li>
      <li>Locked differentials cost more than open ($800 ea vs $550 ea) but eliminate slip failure mode under steam torque</li>
      <li>EWI module + condenser add ~$1,200 combined but give near-unlimited range and reduce water waste to near zero</li>
      <li>250mm ∅ locomotive wheels cost more than Phase 19's smaller wheels — budget for custom cast iron or machined steel</li>
      <li>Phase 20 overall budget is similar to Phase 19 (~$37–41K vs $38–42K) — the changes are mostly value-add swaps, not additions</li>
      <li>Rhombic generator option, if pursued in Phase 21, would add $800–2,000 for the additional crankshaft geometry work</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
